1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,478
Everyone in this party reads the same room.

2
00:00:04,378 --> 00:00:09,596
But one of them came aboard with a question of her own,

3
00:00:10,046 --> 00:00:13,959
and it's listed on her handheld, under her name.

4
00:00:15,759 --> 00:00:17,498
Whose suits are these?

5
00:00:18,398 --> 00:00:22,311
Today you give one person a quest that's theirs,

6
00:00:22,761 --> 00:00:25,370
and you make it lead somewhere.

7
00:00:26,570 --> 00:00:29,178
A side story is a quest.

8
00:00:30,078 --> 00:00:33,991
It has the fields you learned in Class 1,

9
00:00:34,441 --> 00:00:40,963
and it lives in a section of its own, at the end of the file.

10
00:00:42,763 --> 00:00:44,937
What's new is this line.

11
00:00:45,387 --> 00:00:47,561
For, and then a job.

12
00:00:48,461 --> 00:00:53,243
A quest in your Quests section belongs to the whole ship.

13
00:00:53,693 --> 00:00:56,302
This one belongs to one person.

14
00:00:58,102 --> 00:00:59,841
It starts at once,

15
00:01:00,291 --> 00:01:02,030
it has an objective,

16
00:01:02,480 --> 00:01:06,828
and it's done when a signal arrives. Lint warns twice,

17
00:01:07,278 --> 00:01:10,322
and both warnings are true for now.

18
00:01:10,772 --> 00:01:12,946
Nothing sends that signal yet,

19
00:01:13,396 --> 00:01:16,004
and nothing hands the story out.

20
00:01:16,904 --> 00:01:21,252
The word after For is a job from your roster,

21
00:01:21,702 --> 00:01:26,485
or it can be a person: their key, or their name.

22
00:01:27,685 --> 00:01:29,424
So first, the signal.

23
00:01:30,324 --> 00:01:34,237
I find the choice only the surgeon is offered,

24
00:01:34,687 --> 00:01:38,600
and I add a second outcome after the first,

25
00:01:39,050 --> 00:01:44,267
with a comma between them. Learn the fact, comma, send the signal.

26
00:01:45,167 --> 00:01:49,515
The name has to match the story's, letter for letter.

27
00:01:50,415 --> 00:01:52,589
And don't lose that comma.

28
00:01:53,039 --> 00:01:56,083
Without it, the signal is never sent.

29
00:01:57,283 --> 00:01:59,022
Then the handing out.

30
00:01:59,922 --> 00:02:02,096
I open the story file

31
00:02:02,546 --> 00:02:05,589
and find the card from Lecture 2.

32
00:02:06,489 --> 00:02:09,533
One line on it starts the visit,

33
00:02:09,983 --> 00:02:16,070
and I add a few words to the end of that line. Stories equals,

34
00:02:16,520 --> 00:02:21,737
and then the section of the fact sheet to read them from.

35
00:02:22,637 --> 00:02:27,854
The key in quotes is the key on my Side Stories heading.

36
00:02:29,654 --> 00:02:31,393
That's the whole change.

37
00:02:32,293 --> 00:02:37,946
From now on each person is handed their story as they beam down,

38
00:02:38,396 --> 00:02:41,874
and that includes someone who beams down late.

39
00:02:43,074 --> 00:02:45,248
The engineer gets one too,

40
00:02:45,698 --> 00:02:47,872
finished by his own reading.

41
00:02:49,672 --> 00:02:52,715
And a side story can lead on,

42
00:02:53,165 --> 00:02:56,643
the same way any quest does, with Then.

43
00:02:57,543 --> 00:03:01,891
When the surgeon's story completes, it sends a second signal,

44
00:03:02,341 --> 00:03:07,559
and a quest for the whole ship is waiting to hear it.

45
00:03:09,359 --> 00:03:12,402
So read the chain from the top.

46
00:03:12,852 --> 00:03:14,591
She reads the tags.

47
00:03:15,041 --> 00:03:16,780
That finishes her story.

48
00:03:17,230 --> 00:03:19,839
Her story finishes the ship's quest,

49
00:03:20,289 --> 00:03:22,463
and the ship is paid.

50
00:03:23,363 --> 00:03:28,146
A story can carry a reward of its own as well,

51
00:03:28,596 --> 00:03:32,943
and it's paid to the ship that person came from.

52
00:03:34,743 --> 00:03:37,352
The ship's quest gets a page,

53
00:03:37,802 --> 00:03:41,280
because the Quest Log shows all of it.

54
00:03:42,180 --> 00:03:47,398
A heading, and two bullets with a small picture for a dot.

55
00:03:48,298 --> 00:03:51,341
The word after icon names the picture.

56
00:03:53,141 --> 00:03:55,315
The side story stays short.

57
00:03:55,765 --> 00:03:57,939
Tasks only shows its heading.

58
00:03:59,139 --> 00:04:04,791
Four rules. A side story is a bonus, and never the only way,

59
00:04:05,241 --> 00:04:07,850
because nobody covers for a person.

60
00:04:08,750 --> 00:04:11,793
One job word goes in three places:

61
00:04:12,243 --> 00:04:16,591
the roster, the story, and the choice that finishes it.

62
00:04:17,491 --> 00:04:20,535
For takes one job, or one person.

63
00:04:21,435 --> 00:04:24,478
And one story goes to one person.

64
00:04:26,278 --> 00:04:28,017
Lint is good here.

65
00:04:28,467 --> 00:04:32,380
It tells you when a story is for nobody,

66
00:04:32,830 --> 00:04:37,178
and it tells you when two outcomes have run together.

67
00:04:38,378 --> 00:04:43,161
Both aboard. On the doctor's handheld I go back one step,

68
00:04:43,611 --> 00:04:46,220
and there are three apps now,

69
00:04:46,670 --> 00:04:49,278
and the third one is Tasks.

70
00:04:50,178 --> 00:04:52,787
There's her story, under her name.

71
00:04:54,587 --> 00:04:56,326
She reads the tags,

72
00:04:56,776 --> 00:04:59,385
and the bridge is told twice:

73
00:04:59,835 --> 00:05:04,183
her story is complete, and so is the ship's quest.

74
00:05:05,083 --> 00:05:07,691
Then the chief reads his record,

75
00:05:08,141 --> 00:05:10,315
and his story completes too.

76
00:05:12,115 --> 00:05:14,724
Now think about a short crew.

77
00:05:15,624 --> 00:05:18,667
If the doctor stays on the ship,

78
00:05:19,117 --> 00:05:22,161
another console can still take her reading,

79
00:05:22,611 --> 00:05:25,654
but her story was never handed out,

80
00:05:26,104 --> 00:05:28,713
so the ship's quest stays open.

81
00:05:29,613 --> 00:05:33,526
The next lecture shows you the way round that.

82
00:05:34,726 --> 00:05:37,770
Write a story for your third person,

83
00:05:38,220 --> 00:05:40,393
finished by their own reading.

84
00:05:41,293 --> 00:05:45,641
Give the chief's story somewhere to lead. Then break it.

85
00:05:46,091 --> 00:05:48,265
Misspell the job after For,

86
00:05:48,715 --> 00:05:50,454
read what lint says,

87
00:05:50,904 --> 00:05:53,078
and play it once anyway.

88
00:05:54,878 --> 00:05:57,052
Next time is the checkpoint:

89
00:05:57,502 --> 00:06:02,285
one away scene of your own, planned on paper and played.
